ure but risks big loss if opponent has me beat\n4. **All-in (-2):** Maximum pressure but extremely risky given the paired board\n\nReason:\nI'll bet 400 chips for value. My opponent has called three streets, suggesting they have something worth seeing through. If they have a weaker pair or missed draw, they might call a moderate bet. The paired river board makes me cautious about going too large, as sets/full houses are possible. A medium-sized value bet balances extracting value from worse hands while not overcommitting if I'm beat. If opponent raises, I can fold and still have plenty of chips. Given my overall chip lead in the match, controlled aggression is optimal here.\n\nAnswer: 400"}
